  "verbalization": "Golodirsen is implicated in the pathogenesis of Duchenne Muscular Dystrophy (DMD) through a chain of indications that connect it to other muscular dystrophy conditions and therapies. The evidence suggests that Golodirsen is associated with Muscular Dystrophy, which in turn is linked to Eteplirsen and Ataluren, both of which are indicated for DMD. This indicates a potential pathway where Golodirsen may act through a shared mechanism or target a common downstream effect in the treatment of muscular dystrophy. The presence of multiple indirect pathways, each linking Golodirsen to DMD through different therapeutic agents, suggests that the drug may have a broader role in the management of muscular dystrophy, possibly through distinct mechanisms of action or by influencing related pathways. The integration of these indications highlights the complexity of the relationship and the need for further investigation into the specific mechanisms by which Golodirsen contributes to the treatment of DMD.",
